Selenium Basic Assignment 

1. When will you go for Automation Testing?
We go for Automation Testing when the same test cases have to be run repeatedly, especially for regression testing. It is useful when the application is stable, 
needs testing on multiple browsers, and when we want faster and more accurate results while saving time in the long run

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. What is the difference between driver.close() and driver.quit()?
driver.close() closes the current browser window that is being controlled by Selenium. If only one window is open, the browser will close
driver.quit() closes all browser windows opened by Selenium and ends the WebDriver session completely

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.What is the advantage for assigning driver reference in WebDriver interface?
By using WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();, we can easily switch between different browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, etc.) 
by changing only the object creation line, without changing the rest of the code. It also follows polymorphism, making the code more reusable and maintainable

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

